From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stuoningur <50464069+stuoningur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:00:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] generic: mtk_eth_soc: enable the special tag only for the
 MTK tagger

Split the TX_DMA_SPTAG_V3 / MTK_GDMA_SPECIAL_TAG gating out of 795-11
into its own patch (795-12) and use the existing mtk_uses_dsa() helper
instead of open-coding the tag protocol check. mtk_uses_dsa() is moved
up so the TX descriptor path can use it.

This affects every MediaTek board with a non-MTK DSA tagger (MT7622 and
MT7981 boards with RTL8365MB, SmartRG SDG-9000 with MxL86282), see the
patch description.

Drop the "no logic changes" note from 795-11 and refresh 730, 739,
797-01, 750 and 751.
